$\begin{align*}f'(x)&=-2x\\m&=f'(1)=-2\\y-3&=-2(x-1)\\y&=-2x+5\end{align*}$
At the $x$-intercept, $y=0$.
$\begin{align*}0&=-2x+5\\x&=\frac52\end{align*}$
At the $y$-intercept, $x=0$, so $y=5$. Thus $A(\frac52,0)$ and $B(0,5)$.
$\begin{align*}\text{Area}&=\frac12\times\frac52\times5\\&=\frac{25}{4}\text{ square units}\end{align*}$
