$y=x(x-2)$, so the $x$-intercepts are $(0,0)$ and $(2,0)$.
$f'(x)=2x-2$.
At $(0,0)$, the tangent gradient is $-2$.
$\begin{align*}y-0&=-2(x-0)\\y&=-2x\end{align*}$
At $(2,0)$, the tangent gradient is $2$.
$\begin{align*}y-0&=2(x-2)\\y&=2x-4\end{align*}$
Solve the two tangent equations simultaneously.
$\begin{align*}-2x&=2x-4\\4x&=4\\x&=1\\y&=-2(1)=-2\end{align*}$
The tangents intersect at $(1,-2)$.
